cat FR06   # the lower halfword is kept: C2 is replaced by C1 (F2 lemma)
cat FR12   # killed by the core_fetch proof (mutants.py note)
cat FH01   # a fetch is requested with the word in hand (F6)
cat FH03   # held word set on a load edge, never cleared (F4/F1)
cat FH05   # held under a data access in WB (F8, H-L2)
cat FH07   # a fetch behind a branch or jump (R8)
sed fyracore.v s@exwb_trap_cause <= 32'd7;@exwb_trap_cause <= 32'd23;@   # a trap cause of 16 or more (store access fault as 23) is caught by C16
sed fyracore.v s@{1'b1, 31'd7};@{1'b1, 31'd17};@   # an interrupt cause of 16 or more (timer as 17) is caught by C16
